+# Patch 0032: in-app help, pages 13 to 15 (B7)
+
+Items: the 0032 pages from the B7 page plan. Status: `[x]` done and tested in my sandbox, `[ ]` needs you.
+
+## What you asked for
+- Continue B7 with patch 32. Small chunks, three pages per patch, planned in the progress doc and ticked as they are done.
+
+## Steps
+1. [x] Cloned the latest repo (HEAD "Docs Part 4": 0030, 0031 and 0048 to 0053 are all in) and read `DEV_NOTES.md` and `docs/PROGRESS.md` from the clone. The copy of `DEV_NOTES.md` I fetched over the web first is an old one (it stops at the first patches), so everything here comes from the clone.
+2. [x] Read the code behind each page before writing it: `src/screens/Pay.tsx`, `src/screens/CashSheet.tsx`, `src/lib/cashSale.ts`, `src/lib/saleBuilder.ts`, `src/lib/money.ts`, `src/lib/changeScore.ts`, `src/state/cashProfile.ts`, `src/ui/DenomPad.tsx`, `src/ui/kit.tsx` (Keypad), `src/screens/sheets.tsx` (GiftCheckSheet), `src/lib/shopify/giftcards.ts`, `src/lib/giftCode.ts`, `src/lib/saleCodec.ts`, `src/lib/shopify/orderModel.ts`, `src/lib/receiptDoc.ts`, `src/lib/receiptSync.ts`, `src/lib/simpleLabels.ts`.
+3. [x] Ran the real functions to check the numbers in the examples: `allocate` ($10.00 in 3 is 334, 333, 333), `roundCash` (1c and 2c down, 3c and 4c up), `cashTender` (rounded, short and settling cases), `planChange`, `partCashOption` (drawer $20, customer hands $50, bill $37 gives $30 cash and $7 left) and `handBackOptions` (drawer $5, customer hands $20 + $10 + $5, bill $25 gives take $20 + $5, hand back $10).
+4. [x] `help/pay/cash.md`: the Cash received sheet and tap pad, the three outcomes, the change step and its buttons, the red "can't make change" box and its options, skipping the tracking, rounding, what each button writes to the drawer record (table), one flowchart, fault checklist.
+5. [x] `help/pay/gift-card.md`: Check gift card sheet, Use as payment, messages, why the card is charged first, how a code is found (last four characters plus the hidden fingerprint), expiry, receipts, one flowchart, fault checklist.
+6. [x] `help/pay/split-and-part.md`: the Split amount sheet, equal shares and how each payment counts as one share (worked $90 example), part payments by cash, cash plus card and gift card, how the next payment amount is chosen, cancelling, one flowchart, fault checklist.
+7. [x] `help/pay/index.md`: `related` now lists the three new pages and the matching Basic bullets link to them (the "links owed" item from 0031).
+8. [x] `npm run help:build` (15 pages, no problems) and `help/help.json` rewritten. The three new flowcharts also parse with the in-app drawing's own parser.
+9. [x] Tests: `tests/helpdocs.test.ts`, `tests/helpview.test.ts` and `tests/helpcitations.test.ts` (45 tests) pass. No new tests: these are pages only. I could not run the whole suite or `tsc` this time (the full `npm install` fails in my sandbox on the private Zeller registry), but no app code changed.
+10. [x] `docs/PROGRESS.md`: patch log row, the 0032 pages ticked, the links-owed line updated, N21 widened, new question N30, and one correction (below).
+11. [ ] You: N21 now covers these three pages. N30 is a question (below).
+
+## Correction to the progress doc
+The 0019 notes said **Give change but don't track it** records the sale without touching the ledger. The code does not do that: **Done, but don't track it** on the change step still records the notes and coins the customer handed over, and only skips the change given (so the ledger then holds change that has left the drawer). **Exact amount (don't track notes)** does skip both. The cash page describes the real behaviour, and the progress doc line is fixed. I did not change the app. If you would rather the button skipped both, say so and I will make it a small patch.
+
+## Things I noticed while reading the code (not changed here)
+- **Gift card codes on receipts (N30).** A sale paid by gift card prints the full code on the receipt made straight after the sale. Only the last four characters are stored on the Shopify order.
+- **The split rule is untested.** The next payment amount (`target` in `Pay.tsx`) is written inline in the screen, so the only test is for `allocate` in `tests/lib.test.ts`. Pulling it into a small pure function with tests would be an easy follow-up.
+- **Gift card expiry is not checked by the POS.** The sheet shows the date, and Shopify decides at charge time.
+- **A cancelled part-paid sale never credits a gift card back.** Already noted in 0031, repeated on the gift card page.
