    "lead": "The Payment screen is where a sale is paid for. You reach it with **Charge** on the cart (or **Take payment** in the guided checkout). Nothing is taken from the customer until they pay.",
    "sections": {
-    "basic": "### Getting there\nTap **Charge** on the cart. Two checks can come first, only if they apply:\n1. A list of **price adjustments** on the sale, which you keep, change or remove. See [[sales/cart-and-prices]].\n2. **Check these bundles**, if a bundle deal is not a recommended pair. See [[sales/bundles]].\n\nThen the **Payment** screen opens.\n\n### What you see\n- The big number is **Total due**. Once part of the bill is paid it changes to **Remaining**, with *of $…* underneath.\n- Under it, a list of the payments taken so far (card, cash, gift card) and what each paid.\n- The ways to pay. In standard mode the buttons read **Card**, **Cash**, **Gift card** and **Split amount**. In Simple and Minimal modes they read **Pay by card**, **Pay with cash**, **Pay with a gift card** and **Split the payment**, each with a line under it saying what it does, and a heading *How is the customer paying?*\n- If the card reader is not ready you see **Reader issue** in red at the top right. Cash and gift cards still work.\n\n### The four ways to pay\n- **Card**: the customer taps, inserts or swipes on the Zeller terminal. See [[pay/card]].\n- **Cash**: a sheet opens where you tap the notes and coins the customer hands over. It works out the change and which notes and coins to give back.\n- **Gift card**: scan or type the gift card code. The amount taken is the card's balance, or what is still owed, whichever is less. The gift card is charged straight away.\n- **Split amount** (**Split the payment**): take part of the bill one way and the rest another way, or divide it equally. Pick **Split equally 2**, **3** or **4**, or key in the first amount and tap **Continue**. The next payment then says *Next payment: $…*. The amount must be less than what remains. Tap **Cancel split** to go back to paying the lot.\n\nEvery payment taken is added to the list. Pay the rest any way you like, in any order, until **Remaining** reaches $0.00.\n\n### When it is fully paid\nThe sale finishes by itself the moment nothing remains. It is saved and sent to Shopify in the background, and the **Receipt** sheet opens: show a QR code, email or text the link, share it, or tap **No receipt**. Tapping that (or finishing the receipt) clears the cart for the next customer.\n\nIf the total is $0.00 (a free sale), there is one button, **Complete $0.00 sale**.\n\n### Going back\n- **Nothing paid yet:** **Back** returns you to the cart and nothing has changed.\n- **Part paid:** the cart is locked, so you cannot change items, clear it or save it. **Back** asks **Cancel this sale?**. If you choose **Refund & cancel**, card payments are refunded to the customer's card through the terminal. Cash and gift card payments are **not** returned automatically: hand the cash back yourself (the cash drawer record is put back for you) and deal with the gift card by hand.\n- **While the terminal is working** there is no Back button. Use **Cancel** on the *Waiting on terminal* strip first.\n\n### Good to know\n- A cash payment can be rounded to the nearest 5c if **Cash rounding (5c)** is on in Settings ▸ Payments. It only changes the cash amount due, and only when cash pays the whole of what remains. Card amounts are always exact.\n- The register will not lock, and staff cannot be switched, while a card payment is waiting on the terminal.\n- If the iPad is offline the sale is kept on it and sent when it is back online. Card payments need a connection, so they will not work offline, but cash will.",
+    "basic": "### Getting there\nTap **Charge** on the cart. Two checks can come first, only if they apply:\n1. A list of **price adjustments** on the sale, which you keep, change or remove. See [[sales/cart-and-prices]].\n2. **Check these bundles**, if a bundle deal is not a recommended pair. See [[sales/bundles]].\n\nThen the **Payment** screen opens.\n\n### What you see\n- The big number is **Total due**. Once part of the bill is paid it changes to **Remaining**, with *of $…* underneath.\n- Under it, a list of the payments taken so far (card, cash, gift card) and what each paid.\n- The ways to pay. In standard mode the buttons read **Card**, **Cash**, **Gift card** and **Split amount**. In Simple and Minimal modes they read **Pay by card**, **Pay with cash**, **Pay with a gift card** and **Split the payment**, each with a line under it saying what it does, and a heading *How is the customer paying?*\n- If the card reader is not ready you see **Reader issue** in red at the top right. Cash and gift cards still work.\n\n### The four ways to pay\n- **Card**: the customer taps, inserts or swipes on the Zeller terminal. See [[pay/card]].\n- **Cash**: a sheet opens where you tap the notes and coins the customer hands over. It works out the change and which notes and coins to give back. See [[pay/cash]].\n- **Gift card**: scan or type the gift card code. The amount taken is the card's balance, or what is still owed, whichever is less. The gift card is charged straight away. See [[pay/gift-card]].\n- **Split amount** (**Split the payment**): take part of the bill one way and the rest another way, or divide it equally. Pick **Split equally 2**, **3** or **4**, or key in the first amount and tap **Continue**. The next payment then says *Next payment: $…*. The amount must be less than what remains. Tap **Cancel split** to go back to paying the lot. See [[pay/split-and-part]].\n\nEvery payment taken is added to the list. Pay the rest any way you like, in any order, until **Remaining** reaches $0.00.\n\n### When it is fully paid\nThe sale finishes by itself the moment nothing remains. It is saved and sent to Shopify in the background, and the **Receipt** sheet opens: show a QR code, email or text the link, share it, or tap **No receipt**. Tapping that (or finishing the receipt) clears the cart for the next customer.\n\nIf the total is $0.00 (a free sale), there is one button, **Complete $0.00 sale**.\n\n### Going back\n- **Nothing paid yet:** **Back** returns you to the cart and nothing has changed.\n- **Part paid:** the cart is locked, so you cannot change items, clear it or save it. **Back** asks **Cancel this sale?**. If you choose **Refund & cancel**, card payments are refunded to the customer's card through the terminal. Cash and gift card payments are **not** returned automatically: hand the cash back yourself (the cash drawer record is put back for you) and deal with the gift card by hand.\n- **While the terminal is working** there is no Back button. Use **Cancel** on the *Waiting on terminal* strip first.\n\n### Good to know\n- A cash payment can be rounded to the nearest 5c if **Cash rounding (5c)** is on in Settings ▸ Payments. It only changes the cash amount due, and only when cash pays the whole of what remains. Card amounts are always exact.\n- The register will not lock, and staff cannot be switched, while a card payment is waiting on the terminal.\n- If the iPad is offline the sale is kept on it and sent when it is back online. Card payments need a connection, so they will not work offline, but cash will.",
     "deep": "### Part payments and the order they are taken in\nA sale is made of **payments** (the app calls them tenders). Each one has its own amount, and the sale is paid when they add up to the total. You can mix any methods, in any order, and as many as you like. The *Next payment* amount is just the figure the next card, cash or gift card payment will aim for: the split amount, an equal share, or everything that remains.\n\n### Cash rounding in a part-paid sale\nRounding is worked out on the cash that is **due**, not on the amount handed over. If cash pays the whole of what remains, the due amount is rounded to the nearest 5c and the difference is kept on the payment. If cash is only part of the bill, nothing is rounded.\n\n### The gift card is charged first, not last\nWhen you choose a gift card, the amount is taken off the card's balance straight away, before the sale finishes. If Shopify cannot do it you see **Gift card could not be charged** with the reason, and nothing is added to the sale. This is why cancelling a part-paid sale does not give the money back to a gift card by itself.\n\n### What \"finished\" means\nWhen the last payment makes **Remaining** $0.00, the app builds the sale record, takes the sold units off the stock count on this iPad, puts the sale in a queue for Shopify, and, if the sale started from a saved cart, removes that saved cart. The queue creates the Shopify order and adjusts Shopify's stock. If that fails or the iPad is offline, the sale stays queued and is retried. You can see how many are waiting in More ▸ Support & diagnostics ▸ Sync.\n\n### Why the cart locks\nOnce any payment is on the sale, changing the cart would make what was paid and what is owed disagree. So the lines, the keypad, Save cart and Clear cart all say **Payment in progress** until the sale is paid or cancelled.",
     "advanced": "### From Charge to a finished sale\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  A[Charge in CartPane.tsx or Take payment in GuidedCheckout.tsx] --> B[Pay.tsx: remaining = total minus paidTotal]\n  B --> C{which button}\n  C -->|card| D[runCard: see the card page]\n  C -->|cash| E[CashSheet then takeCash]\n  C -->|gift card| F[GiftCheckSheet then useGift debits the card]\n  C -->|split| G[chunk or equalLeft sets the next payment amount]\n  D --> H[addTender adds to cart.tenders]\n  E --> H\n  F --> H\n  G --> B\n  H --> I{remaining is 0?}\n  I -->|no| B\n  I -->|yes| J[buildSale then applyLocalStock then recordSale]\n  J --> K[ReceiptPrompt then finishAll empties the cart]\n```\n\n### Where the code is\n| Job | Where |\n|---|---|\n| The screen and all its state | `Pay` in `src/screens/Pay.tsx` |\n| Total, what is paid, what remains | `usePriced` in `src/state/selectors.ts` gives the total; `paidTotal` in `src/lib/saleBuilder.ts` adds up the payments; `Pay` itself works out what remains |\n| Building a payment | `cardTender`, `cashTender` in `src/lib/saleBuilder.ts`; the gift card payment is built in `useGift` in `Pay.tsx` |\n| Finishing | the `finalising` effect in `Pay.tsx`: `buildSale`, `applyLocalStock`, `recordSale` (`src/lib/saleBuilder.ts`, `src/lib/sync.ts`) |\n| Cash ledger | `postCashSale`, `reverseCashTender`, `cashDue` in `src/lib/cashSale.ts` |\n| Cancelling a part-paid sale | `abandon` in `Pay.tsx` |\n| Which card states may use a sheet | `showsOwnSheet`, `showsWaitingStrip`, `lockPayButtons` in `src/lib/payUi.ts` |\n| Simple mode wording | `payTitle`, `payHint`, `payQuestion` in `src/lib/simpleLabels.ts` |\n| Receipt step | `ReceiptPrompt` in `src/screens/Receipt.tsx` |\n\nThe payments live on the cart as `cart.tenders`, so they survive leaving the screen and are what locks the cart. The sale's id (`cart.saleUuid`) is made at the first payment and kept until the sale is paid or cancelled. Card attempt references are built from it, which is how a payment can be matched to its sale later.\n\nThe finishing effect runs once (a `finalising` flag stops it repeating) when there is at least one payment, nothing remains, and the terminal is not waiting. The flag is only cleared by `finishAll`.\n\n### Reading the code for a fault\n- **Pay by card, Cash, Gift card and Split are all greyed out.** `lockPayButtons` is true while the card phase is waiting. If the app was closed mid-payment, reopen the Payment screen: the waiting state is not saved, but the attempt is. Check the card page for what happens to an unfinished attempt.\n- **Paid in full but the sale did not finish.** The effect holds off while the card phase is `waiting`. Look for the strip at the top of the screen.\n- **Cart is stuck as \"Payment in progress\" with nothing paid.** Something left a payment in `cart.tenders`. Open Payment and use **Back**, then **Refund & cancel**.\n- **Sale is finished but missing in Shopify.** It is in the queue: More ▸ Support & diagnostics ▸ Sync shows how many are waiting and the last error, and **Sync now** retries.\n- **A free sale has no payment buttons.** Expected: only **Complete $0.00 sale** shows, and it adds a $0 cash payment.\n- **Tests.** `tests/payui.test.ts` (which card states may draw a sheet), `tests/sale.test.ts` and `tests/cashsale.test.ts` (building sales and cash payments), `tests/simplelabels.test.ts` (Simple mode wording)."
    }
@@ -65,6 +68,99 @@
     "advanced": "### What happens when you tap Card\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  A[runCard in Pay.tsx] --> B{buttons locked or an unknown attempt on this sale}\n  B -->|unknown attempt| C[Payment status unknown sheet]\n  B -->|no| D{terminal ready}\n  D -->|no| E[checkReader in zellerBridge.tsx]\n  E -->|still no| F[Reader sheet]\n  D -->|yes| G[attemptRef then onStarted saves the attempt as started]\n  E -->|ready| G\n  G --> H[startCharge in zeller.ts calls terminal.purchase]\n  H --> I[normalise turns the SDK result into a PaymentResult]\n  I -->|APPROVED| J[cardTender then addTender]\n  I -->|DECLINED| K[Not approved sheet]\n  I -->|CANCELLED| L[back to idle]\n  I -->|NOT_READY| F\n  I -->|UNKNOWN| M[recheck: reconcile up to 6 times 4 s apart]\n  M -->|approved| J\n  M -->|declined or cancelled| K\n  M -->|no answer| C\n```\n\n### Where the code is\n| Job | Where |\n|---|---|\n| The flow, sheets and strip | `runCard`, `recheck`, `manualResolve` in `src/screens/Pay.tsx` |\n| Which states may draw a sheet | `showsOwnSheet`, `showsWaitingStrip`, `lockPayButtons` in `src/lib/payUi.ts` |\n| Talking to the SDK | `startCharge`, `startRefund`, `reconcile`, `normalise`, `describeEvent` in `src/lib/zeller.ts` |\n| One terminal for the whole app | `ZellerRoot`, `getTerminal`, `checkReader`, `pairReader` in `src/zellerBridge.tsx` |\n| Code to message | `RESPONSE_CODES`, `lookupResponse` in `src/lib/responseCodes.ts` |\n| Fees | `feeFor`, `feeRateFor` in `src/lib/fees.ts`; `cardTender` in `src/lib/saleBuilder.ts` |\n| Pairing, test purchase, attempts list | `src/screens/Diagnostics.tsx` |\n| Saved attempts | `Attempt` in `src/state/store.ts` (`pos.attempts`) |\n| Locking while waiting | `paymentActive` in `src/lib/screensaver.ts`, used by `lockDecision` in `src/lib/posLock.ts` and by staff switching in `src/lib/staffAuth.ts` |\n\nThe SDK returns errors instead of throwing them. `normalise` turns either kind of result into one of five outcomes: `APPROVED`, `DECLINED`, `CANCELLED`, `UNKNOWN` or `NOT_READY`, and nothing outside `zeller.ts` reads a raw SDK result. A network or connection failure is `NOT_READY` when the terminal had not started, and `UNKNOWN` once it had.\n\n`startCharge` does one more thing before it returns. If the result is cancelled or unknown, or a decline arrived after the terminal had started processing, it calls `reconcile`, which looks the reference up with `getTransactions`. An approved match turns the result into `APPROVED`. That lookup is what makes Cancel safe.\n\nThe attempt's status moves `started`, then `approved`, `declined`, `cancelled`, `unknown` or `resolved`. A **started** attempt keeps `paymentActive` true for five minutes, which is what blocks locking and staff switching; an attempt left at **started** by a closed app stops blocking after that. The waiting state itself is not saved, so reopening Payment shows the buttons again, but an `unknown` attempt on the sale still blocks **Card** through `blockedByUnknown`.\n\nEvents are written to the history CSV with `csv.event`: `declined`, `cancelled`, `unknown_payment`, `unknown_resolved`, `refund_failed` and `void`.\n\n### Reading the code for a fault\n- **Card button does nothing.** The amount is $0 (`runCard` returns when it is 0 or less), the buttons are locked by a waiting card phase, or an `unknown` attempt exists for this sale.\n- **\"Reader issue\" that will not clear.** In More ▸ Support & diagnostics tap **Check reader**: it calls `initialise` on the terminal. `Setup Required` means pair it. `Network Failure` shows as *Reader offline — no internet*.\n- **The customer was charged but the sale shows no card payment.** It is an `unknown` attempt: check **Card attempts (this device)** in Support & diagnostics (the last eight, with their reference and who resolved them) and look for the same reference in the Zeller dashboard. The reference is the sale id followed by the attempt number.\n- **A decline message is vague.** The code is not in `RESPONSE_CODES`, so the SDK's own text is shown. Add it there if you want better wording.\n- **The reader says busy.** *Paired Device Busy* means another register is using the terminal. Only one register can charge at a time.\n- **Tests.** `tests/lib.test.ts` covers the response codes, fees, `normalise`, and `startCharge` (approve; a cancel after processing that still approves through `reconcile`; a timeout that stays unknown; a decline that keeps the cart) and `startRefund`. `tests/payui.test.ts` covers which states may draw a sheet."
    }
